    "policy": "W13 and W44 showed a three-output video batch with a failed slot and its separate retry. Video profiles produce one output and the workspace always sends outputCount 1, so no one can reach that state. W12 covers a failed video and its Retry; the retried request then shows the ordinary generating state. The Request failure Slot variant and both Start here review links were removed with the screens. Do not redraw video batch slots; image batches stay in C09 and C30. Later the same day W14 (\"Cancellation requires an explicit action\", a Cancel this generation? dialog) was deleted. Nothing in the design opened it once the Request status card and its Cancel buttons were removed, and the app has no cancel route or control, so cancellation stays an internal contract. Later on October 16, W06 (\"Accepted request queued; captured words are read-only\") and W54 (\"Several accepted requests retain separate status\") were deleted. Their only difference from W07 was a queued line (\"Queued\", \"Lower camera · queued\"): the server's not-started job status, which a person cannot see or act on. W07 shows a running request with its read-only words. Do not redraw queued status lines.",
